  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>34</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long ladder weighing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> leans on a frictionless wall. Its feet rest on the floor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away from the wall as shown in the figure. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></math> are the reaction forces of the floor and the wall, then ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mfrac></math> will be :<br />(Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0082_fd9415b5ab80.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 220px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>110</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>113</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>109</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
